<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Cheng of Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 671–626 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Cheng of Chu ruled the southern Chinese state of Chu from 671 to 626 BCE. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wen-of-chu">King Wen of Chu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xi-gui">Xi Gui</a>, the captured lady of Xi, he expanded Chu's power north towards the central plain until his army was defeated by Jin at Chengpu in 632 BCE. He was forced to kill himself in 626 BCE by his son, the future King Mu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-cheng-of-chu.jpg" alt="King Cheng of Chu" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuan Fuying 阮福影 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zheng_Mao.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
